### =====================================================================
### cart-service - ready-to-run requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8107, so we send the X-User-* / X-Store-Id headers
### ourselves (normally the API gateway adds them from the JWT).
### Adding products and checking out call product-read-service (port 8105): keep it running.
###
### Seed data (docs/seed-data.md):
###   customer1 (user 4) has a Fresh Mart cart: Tomato x2, Amul Taaza Milk x3, Farm Eggs x1 = 201.00
###   coupons WELCOME50, SAVE10 (platform), FRESH20 (store 1), GREEN30 (store 2),
###           SUMMER25 (expired), MANGO15 (switched off)
###   delivery fee 30.00 below 299.00, minimum order 99.00
### Run the requests in order: the last ones put customer1's cart back to the seed state.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8107


### 1. CUSTOMER (user 4): my cart -> items total 201.00 + delivery 30.00 = 231.00
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 2. PUBLIC: offers usable at Fresh Mart (platform coupons + FRESH20; no expired or switched-off ones)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coupons?storeId=1


### 3. CUSTOMER (user 4): add 1 dozen bananas (60.00) -> 261.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "productId": 4,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 4. CUSTOMER (user 4): Organic Spinach is sold by Green Basket (store 2) -> 409, one store per cart
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "productId": 11,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 5. CUSTOMER (user 4): FRESH20 = 20 % of 261.00 = 52.20 -> payable 261.00 - 52.20 + 30.00 = 238.80
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "code": "fresh20"
}


### 6. CUSTOMER (user 4): SUMMER25 has expired -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "code": "SUMMER25"
}


### 7. CUSTOMER (user 4): GREEN30 belongs to another store -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "code": "GREEN30"
}


### 8. CUSTOMER (user 4): 3 dozen bananas -> 381.00: free delivery, FRESH20 capped at 60.00 -> payable 321.00
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items/4
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "quantity": 3
}


### 9. CUSTOMER (user 4): remove the bananas -> 201.00: FRESH20 needs 249.00, the cart explains why it gives 0 now
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items/4
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 10. CUSTOMER (user 4): checkout page -> readyForCheckout false, the problem is listed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/checkout
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 11. CUSTOMER (user 4): remove the coupon (cart is back to the seed state)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 12. INTERNAL (order-service): checkout summary for user 4 -> readyForCheckout true, today's prices
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/carts/4/checkout


### 13. CUSTOMER (user 7): add 2 x Organic Spinach from Green Basket (first item creates the cart)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "productId": 11,
  "quantity": 2
}


### 14. CUSTOMER (user 7): switch to Fresh Mart: replaceCart=true empties the Green Basket cart first
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items?replaceCart=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "productId": 2,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 15. CUSTOMER (user 7): empty my cart
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 16. VENDOR (store 1): my coupons -> FRESH20 and MANGO15
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/coupons
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 17. VENDOR (store 1): a new weekend offer (run once; a second run gives 409 "already taken")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/coupons
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "code": "WEEKEND40",
  "description": "Fresh Mart weekend: flat 40 off on 399 or more",
  "discountType": "FLAT",
  "discountValue": 40.00,
  "minOrderAmount": 399.00,
  "validFrom": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
  "validUntil": "2027-03-31T23:59:59Z",
  "usageLimit": 200,
  "perCustomerLimit": 2
}


### 18. VENDOR (store 1): invalid coupon -> 400 with one error per field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/coupons
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "code": "X!",
  "description": "",
  "discountType": "PERCENTAGE",
  "discountValue": 0,
  "minOrderAmount": -1,
  "validFrom": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
  "validUntil": "2027-03-31T23:59:59Z"
}


### 19. ADMIN: platform coupons only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coupons?platformOnly=true
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 20. ADMIN: a store coupon cannot be edited by an admin (only switched on/off) -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coupons/3
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "code": "FRESH20",
  "description": "Changed by admin",
  "discountType": "PERCENTAGE",
  "discountValue": 50,
  "minOrderAmount": 0,
  "validFrom": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "validUntil": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
}
